    "title": "Strategists: GOP Must Move Past Social Issues, Focus on the Economy",
    "text": "Democrats saw sweeping wins in several key state elections—including Virginia and New Jersey—amid voter frustration over the government shutdown and economic concerns. Gerard Filitti, political strategist and attorney, and Robin Biro, Democratic strategist and former Obama regional campaign director, joined NTD to discuss what the election results mean for both parties, the GOP’s messaging challenges, and how these outcomes could shape the 2026 elections and beyond.\nStrategists: GOP Must Move Past Social Issues, Focus on the Economy\nGerard Filitti and Robin Biro discussed what the election results mean for both parties, GOP messaging challenges, and how the outcomes could shape the 2026 midterm.\n|\nPublished: 11/5/2025, 11:59:05 PM EST",
